  "id": "motor-planning",
  "term": "motor planning",
  "definition": "Motor planning is the process of preparing a movement in advance based on sensory information and the demands of the task. It includes selecting and specifying how the movement will be carried out so the body can produce the needed motor commands, especially when there is more than one possible way to reach a goal.",
